# =====================================================================
# ✒ Metadata
#     - Title: Agent Watch Ignore Rules (dd1 Tools Edition - v1.0)
#     - File Name: .gitignore
#     - Relative Path: .gitignore
#     - Artifact Type: config
#     - Version: 1.0.0
#     - Date: 11/16/2026
#     - Update: Monday, November 16, 2026
#     - Author: Dennis 'dendogg' Smaltz
#     - A.I. Acknowledgement: Anthropic - Claude Opus 5.5
#     - Signature: ︻デ═─── ✦ ✦ ✦ | Aim Twice, Shoot Once!
#
# ✒ Description:
#     What git never takes from an agent-watch checkout. The tool has no
#     dependencies and writes its state outside the repository, so most of
#     these rules guard against what a person or another tool leaves
#     behind: transcripts copied in to debug, secrets, editor and OS files.
#
# ✒ Key Features:
#     - Claude Code transcripts (*.jsonl) are never committed: they hold
#       prompts and tool output, which is exactly what this tool reads
#     - Secrets and machine-local settings: .env files, keys, .npmrc,
#       Claude Code's settings.local.json and CLAUDE.local.md
#     - agent-watch's own state, in case AGENT_WATCH_STATE points here:
#       state.json, the log, notices.json, archive/ and criteria/
#     - Dependency trees and lockfiles: there are no dependencies to lock
#     - Test and coverage output, npm pack tarballs, handoff reports
#     - Inkscape backups and autosaves of the logo's master
#     - Editor, OS and temp leftovers for Windows, macOS and Linux
#
# ✒ Other Important Information:
#     - Dependencies: git 2.x
#     - Compatible platforms: any git client
#     - `git check-ignore -v <path>` names the rule that matched a path.
#     - Per-machine exclusions belong in .git/info/exclude, not here.
# ---------
# =====================================================================

# --- Claude Code transcripts ------------------------------------------------
# A session transcript holds the person's prompts and every tool's output.
# The suite builds its fixtures in the OS temp folder, so none belongs here.
*.jsonl

# --- Secrets and machine-local settings ------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.npmrc
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# --- agent-watch state, if AGENT_WATCH_STATE points into the checkout -------
# By default it lives in %LOCALAPPDATA%\agent-watch on Windows and
# ~/.local/state/agent-watch elsewhere.
/state.json
/agent-watch.log
/notices.json
/archive/
/criteria/

# --- Dependencies and package-manager output -------------------------------
# agent-watch uses Node's own modules only; nothing is installed.
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
.pnp.*
.yarn/
.npm/
package-lock.json
npm-shrinkwrap.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.tgz
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- Logs, reports and test output ----------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov
test-results/
playwright-report/
captures/
shots/
/handoff*.md
/handoff*.json

# --- Inkscape leftovers from editing the logo -------------------------------
*.svg.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9]_[0-9][0-9]_*.svg
_autosaves/

# --- Editors ----------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.history/
*.code-workspace
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Operating systems ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# --- Temp and merge leftovers ----------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
